<%# The look of a yes-or-no value (boolean), wherever it is on the sheet: its name, then a classic switch, the look
    of shared/_switch (decision: track field-line when off, primary when on, knob in primary-ink). Unlike that
    component, it is a real check box (role="switch", hidden under the track and the knob, which follow it by
    peer-checked:): sent with the form, usable with the keyboard, no JavaScript needed. The hidden "0" first: an
    unchecked box sends nothing on its own. "1" or "0" (CharacterSheets::Builder) %>
<div class="mt-1 flex w-full items-center gap-3">
  <label for="<%= sheet_field_id(field) %>" class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink"><%= field["label"] %></label>
  <span class="relative inline-flex">
    <%= hidden_field_tag sheet_field_name(field), "0", id: nil %>
    <%= check_box_tag sheet_field_name(field), "1", character.sheet[field["key"]] == true,
                      id: sheet_field_id(field), role: "switch", class: "peer absolute inset-0 z-10 cursor-pointer opacity-0" %>
    <span aria-hidden="true" class="<%= switch_track_classes %>"></span>
    <span aria-hidden="true" class="<%= switch_knob_classes %>"></span>
  </span>
</div>
